Tier is informal: the game does not gate biomes explicitly, but attempting a Tier 4 biome with Tier 1 gear ends predictably.

== Progression path ==

A typical early-game progression:

# Spawn in '''[[Mossy Forest]]'''. Build a base, craft a [[Campfire]], survive a few nights.
# Push into '''[[Mountain Forest]]''' for Iron and Coal. Unlock [[Furnace]] + [[Anvil Workbench]] and metal weapons.
# Detour to '''[[Tropical Jungle]]''' or '''[[Tropical Swamp]]''' for [[Biochemical Workbench]] reagents.
# Scavenge '''[[Winter Town]]''' or '''[[Desert]]''' for mid-tier salvage and vehicle parts.
# End-game: '''[[Wasteland]]''' and '''[[Warzone]]''' for the top-tier loot.

== Points of interest by biome ==

Each biome contains scripted POIs: pre-built structures with high-density loot and elevated threat. See [[Locations]] for the full list. Notable examples:

* '''Forest (Mossy Forest):''' [[Airport]], [[Mall]], [[Pool]], [[School]], [[Diner]]
* '''[[Mountain Forest]]:''' [[Country House]], [[Country House II]], [[AV House]], [[Factory Zone]]
* '''[[Warzone]]:''' [[Warzone Buildings]] (dense ruined-city cluster)

== Loot crates ==

Every biome has its own crate variant with biome-appropriate loot:

* [[Forest Loot Crate]] · [[Mossy Loot Crate]] · [[Mountain Loot Crate]] · [[Desert Loot Crate]] · [[Snowy Loot Crate]] · [[Swamp Loot Crate]] · [[Warzone Loot Crate]]

== Vehicles ==

Vehicle chassis are biome-native: the game ships six vehicle sets, one per biome variant. See [[Vehicles]].

